# The vcpkg libraries the Windows release links and ships (canon row 248: the same set as the Mac's tools/deps/deps.pin).
# BASELINE is the commit of github.com/microsoft/vcpkg the box's C:\vcpkg was at when they were built (2026-11-23, the machine set up that day; before it 29718cfe of 2026-11-05); the
# ports below are what that commit installs for the x64-windows triplet. To reproduce on a fresh machine:
#   git -C C:\vcpkg checkout <BASELINE>;  C:\vcpkg\vcpkg.exe install opencolorio openexr "libjpeg-turbo[turbojpeg]" "tiff[tools]" --triplet x64-windows
# packaging\windows\make-msix.ps1 REFUSES to pack when an installed port differs from this file (through the notices'
# .check sidecar, which carries these lines), and the Windows notices print these versions.
# One known difference from the Mac: OpenEXR is 3.5.4 here (the Mac builds 3.5.3, tools/deps/deps.pin).
# libjpeg-turbo is 3.2.1 on both systems since this baseline; `cargo test -p min-image` passes the same pixel fixtures.
BASELINE=3cb3f66bb768e04b8af95737adaaec3b4a583842
opencolorio=2.6.0
openexr=3.5.4
imath=3.2.3#1
libjpeg-turbo=3.2.1#1
tiff=4.7.2
yaml-cpp=0.9.0#1
expat=2.10.0
pystring=1.2.0
minizip-ng=4.1.0
zlib=1.4
libdeflate=1.26
openjph=0.32.0#1
zstd=1.5.7
liblzma=5.8.4
bzip2=1.0.8#6
libspng=0.7.4#1
